{
  "method": "Input.scroll",
  "description": "Performs explicit scrolling: scrolls by a requested distance or to a boundary, brings an element into view for inspection, or reads the current scroll state. The target form accepts an optional container and excludes coordinates and displacement. For displacement, boundary, or state reads, use container or paired x/y; omit both to use the page viewport. axis requires edge; edge excludes deltas. Reports the observed result and whether the requested scroll goal was reached. For a known interaction target, call its locator-based Input Action directly.",
  "requiresPurpose": true,
  "catalogRevision": "sha256:f14f45a51d9e8c2fec30ee6e50e9cd2003d0d7eb9b217ea8922884f5fa221f76",
